<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-362] Parquet buffered writer is too sensitive regarding unions and unknown fields</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-362</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Parquet does prevent records with unknown union fields to be written as it would create a TProtocol violation. But it also prevents records with unions having one their field itself having an unknown field (which is acceptable if it is a struct).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The recursive check should be removed, and only when a union field is unknown should the record be deemed invalid.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
